2324	    // CM=64 path (1 consumer WG) frees smem for a deeper STAGES=4 ring but loses the 2nd consumer
2325	    // warpgroup -> only 8 warps/SM (vs 12), measuring 0.72x: occupancy, not ring depth, is the binding
2326	    // constraint, and acc_o[128] hard-caps it at 1 CTA/SM. A head-dim-split (2 WGs on the same rows,
2327	    // each owning half of HDV at acc_o[64]) restores 12 warps + STAGES=4, but pays either a 1.5x
2328	    // redundant-QK cost or an asymmetric P-via-smem rewrite -- neither cleanly beats CM=128's 0.85x.
